      "lemma": "qa`niTiyn",
      "lemma_arabic": "قَٰنِطِين",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "15:55",
      "ayah_arabic": "قَالُواْ بَشَّرۡنَٰكَ بِٱلۡحَقِّ فَلَا تَكُن مِّنَ ٱلۡقَٰنِطِينَ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Al-Hijr",
      "literal_gloss": "the despairing",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "They said, \"We have given you good tidings in truth, so do not be of the despairing.\"",
        "pickthall": "They said: We bring thee good tidings in truth. So be not thou of the despairing.",
        "khattab": "They responded, “We give you good news in all truth, so do not be one of those who despair.”",
        "arberry": "give me good tidings?' They said, 'We give thee good tidings of truth. Be not of those that despair.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        15,
        56,
        3
      ],
      "form_arabic": "يَقْنَطُ",
      "lemma": "qanaTu",
      "lemma_arabic": "قَنَطُ",
      "pos": "V",
      "ayah_id": "15:56",
      "ayah_arabic": "قَالَ وَمَن يَقۡنَطُ مِن رَّحۡمَةِ رَبِّهِۦٓ إِلَّا ٱلضَّآلُّونَ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Al-Hijr",
      "literal_gloss": "despairs",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "He said, \"And who despairs of the mercy of his Lord except for those astray?\"",
        "pickthall": "He said: And who despaireth of the mercy of his Lord save those who are astray?",
        "khattab": "He exclaimed, “Who would despair of the mercy of their Lord except the misguided?”",
        "arberry": "He said, 'And who despairs of the mercy of his Lord, excepting those that are astray?'"
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        30,
        36,
        15
      ],
      "form_arabic": "يَقْنَطُونَ",
      "lemma": "qanaTu",
      "lemma_arabic": "قَنَطُ",
      "pos": "V",
      "ayah_id": "30:36",
      "ayah_arabic": "وَإِذَآ أَذَقۡنَا ٱلنَّاسَ رَحۡمَةࣰ فَرِحُواْ بِهَاۖ وَإِن تُصِبۡهُمۡ سَيِّئَةُۢ بِمَا قَدَّمَتۡ أَيۡدِيهِمۡ إِذَا هُمۡ يَقۡنَطُونَ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Ar-Room",
      "literal_gloss": "despair",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "And when We let the people taste mercy, they rejoice therein, but if evil afflicts them for what their hands have put forth, immediately they despair.",
        "pickthall": "And when We cause mankind to taste of mercy they rejoice therein; but if an evil thing befall them as the consequence of their own deeds, lo! they are in despair!",
        "khattab": "If We give people a taste of mercy, they become prideful ˹because˺ of it. But if they are afflicted with an evil for what their hands have done, they instantly fall into despair",
        "arberry": "And when We let men taste mercy, they rejoice in it; but if some evil befalls them for that their own hands have forwarded, behold, they despair."
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        39,
        53,
        8
      ],
      "form_arabic": "تَقْنَطُوا@",
      "lemma": "qanaTu",
      "lemma_arabic": "قَنَطُ",
      "pos": "V",
      "ayah_id": "39:53",
      "ayah_arabic": "۞قُلۡ يَٰعِبَادِيَ ٱلَّذِينَ أَسۡرَفُواْ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمۡ لَا تَقۡنَطُواْ مِن رَّحۡمَةِ ٱللَّهِۚ إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ يَغۡفِرُ ٱلذُّنُوبَ جَمِيعًاۚ إِنَّهُۥ هُوَ ٱلۡغَفُورُ ٱلرَّحِيمُ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Az-Zumar",
      "literal_gloss": "despair",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "Say, \"O My servants who have transgressed against themselves [by sinning], do not despair of the mercy of Allah. Indeed, Allah forgives all sins. Indeed, it is He who is the Forgiving, the Merciful.\"",
        "pickthall": "Say: O My slaves who have been prodigal to their own hurt! Despair not of the mercy of Allah, Who forgiveth all sins. Lo! He is the Forgiving, the Merciful.",
        "khattab": "Say, ˹O Prophet, that Allah says,˺ “O My servants who have exceeded the limits against their souls! Do not lose hope in Allah’s mercy, for Allah certainly forgives all sins. He is indeed the All-Forgiving, Most Merciful",
        "arberry": "Say: 'O my people who have been prodigal against yourselves, do not despair of God's mercy; surely God forgives sins altogether; surely He is the All-forgiving, the All-compassionate."
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        41,
        49,
        11
      ],
      "form_arabic": "قَنُوطٌ",
      "lemma": "qanuwT",
      "lemma_arabic": "قَنُوط",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "41:49",
      "ayah_arabic": "لَّا يَسۡـَٔمُ ٱلۡإِنسَٰنُ مِن دُعَآءِ ٱلۡخَيۡرِ وَإِن مَّسَّهُ ٱلشَّرُّ فَيَـُٔوسࣱ قَنُوطࣱ‏",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Fussilat",
      "literal_gloss": "(and) despairs",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "Man is not weary of supplication for good [things], but if evil touches him, he is hopeless and despairing.",
        "pickthall": "Man tireth not of praying for good, and if ill toucheth him, then he is disheartened, desperate.",
        "khattab": "One never tires of praying for good. And if touched with evil, they become desperate and hopeless",
        "arberry": "Man wearies not of praying for good; but when evil visits him, then he is cast down and desperate."
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        42,
        28,
        8
      ],
      "form_arabic": "قَنَطُوا@",
      "lemma": "qanaTu",
      "lemma_arabic": "قَنَطُ",
      "pos": "V",
      "ayah_id": "42:28",
      "ayah_arabic": "وَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي يُنَزِّلُ ٱلۡغَيۡثَ مِنۢ بَعۡدِ مَا قَنَطُواْ وَيَنشُرُ رَحۡمَتَهُۥۚ وَهُوَ ٱلۡوَلِيُّ ٱلۡحَمِيدُ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Ash-Shura",
      "literal_gloss": "they have despaired",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "And it is He who sends down the rain after they had despaired and spreads His mercy. And He is the Protector, the Praiseworthy.",
        "pickthall": "And He it is Who sendeth down the saving rain after they have despaired, and spreadeth out His mercy. He is the Protecting Friend, the Praiseworthy.",
        "khattab": "He is the One Who sends down rain after people have given up hope, spreading out His mercy. He is the Guardian, the Praiseworthy",
        "arberry": "And it is He who sends down the rain after they have despaired, and He unfolds His mercy; He is the Protector, the All-laudable."
      }
    }
  ]
